# {{ project_slug }}

An AI/BI Genie Space and Lakeview dashboard over a metric view built on the TPCH sample dataset, deployed as a Databricks Asset Bundle.

## Prerequisites

- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/install.html) v0.230+, authenticated (`databricks auth login`)
- A Unity Catalog-enabled workspace with access to `samples.tpch`
- Permission to create catalogs in the metastore — the bundle creates catalog `{{ cfg.catalog }}` (or your override) on deploy

## What's here

```
notebooks/setup_metric_views.py         # Creates the v_tpch metric view (run before opening dashboard/Genie)
resources/
├── jobs/setup_views_job.yml            # Job running the setup notebook on serverless compute
├── dashboards/tpch_overview.lvdash.json # Lakeview dashboard
└── genie_spaces/tpch_genie.genie_space.yml
```

## Deploy

```bash
databricks bundle validate --target dev
databricks bundle deploy --target dev
databricks bundle run {{ project_slug | replace("-", "_") }}_setup_views --target dev
```

Run the setup job once before opening the dashboard or Genie Space — both depend on the `v_tpch` metric view existing.

## Deploy-time catalog/schema override

The setup job and Genie Space resolve `catalog`/`schema` from bundle variables, so they can point at a different catalog without regenerating the project:

```bash
databricks bundle deploy --target prod --var catalog=prod_catalog --var schema=tpch_metrics
```

The Lakeview dashboard is the one exception — its queries are baked to `{{ cfg.catalog }}.{{ cfg.schema }}` at scaffold time (dashboard JSON isn't variable-substituted by DAB). Edit `resources/dashboards/tpch_overview.lvdash.json` directly if you need it pointed elsewhere.

## Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `catalog` | `{{ cfg.catalog }}` | Catalog for the `v_tpch` metric view |
| `schema` | `{{ cfg.schema }}` | Schema for the `v_tpch` metric view |

## Troubleshooting

- **Dashboard/Genie show no data** — run the setup job first; both query the `v_tpch` metric view it creates.
- **"Catalog does not exist"** — create `{{ cfg.catalog }}` (or your override) before deploying.
